// Deployment pipeline, run by the Jenkins of a yggdrasil installation. Keep this file named
// Jenkinsfile, at the repository's root, and replace <application-id> with exactly this
// application's id in that installation's catalog.yaml (the build fails otherwise).
//
// All the logic lives in yggdrasil's shared library; what deploys where comes from the catalog:
//   - a push to a branch that an environment's `branches` match deploys there (trigger: branch);
//   - Build with Parameters > DEPLOY_TO deploys to a trigger: manual environment that has an agent;
//   - a green release/x.y.z -> main pull request deploys to every release environment in order,
//     then is merged, tagged and released as vx.y.z (only if the application has one).
// Build and test stay in GitHub Actions; this file only deploys.

@Library('yggdrasil') _

yggdrasilPipeline(stack: '<application-id>')
